course: dictionary
lesson: 4009
title: Gardener and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gardener is a person who looks after a garden and its plants. You can often work out a new word from the words around it, which are its context. «Many animals live right next to us, and robins follow gardeners for worms» tells you that gardeners work outside, where worms and animals are too.
explain: Gardeners do many jobs. They dig, weed and mow, and they plant rows of flowers or trees. Try the check: swap your meaning into the sentence. «Robins follow a person who looks after a garden and its plants for worms» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Some gardeners work for a living, and some garden just for fun. A gardener can also be a character in a story, such as the gardener in a big house or a secret garden. When the clues are not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A gardener is a person who looks after a garden and its plants.
fact: Gardeners can work as a job, or garden just for fun.
fact: «Gardeners» is the plural, which means more than one gardener.
fact: Gardeners plant rows of flowers or trees, dig, weed and mow.
fact: Gardeners know plants need water, light and soil, and they compost waste.
exercise: «Many animals live right next to us, and robins follow gardeners for worms.» What is a gardener? | A large house with many rooms | A kind of bird | *A person who looks after a garden and its plants | An animal that digs for worms
exercise: Which of these is a job a gardener does? | Baking bread in a shop | Driving a bus across town | *Weeding and mowing the lawn | Taking tickets on a train
exercise: What do gardeners do in the garden? | Drive cars to work | Sell fish at the market | *Plant rows of flowers and trees | Sing songs to the moon
test: «The Rabbit and his gardener Pat argue about the giant arm in the window.» Who is the gardener in this sentence? | The Rabbit | The arm | The window | *Pat
test: Which word is the plural, meaning more than one gardener? | *gardeners | garden's | gardening | garden
exam: «Gardeners know plants need water, light and soil.» Which clue helps you work out what gardener means? | The word need, which means to be hungry | *Plants and soil, which a garden has | The word know, which means to be sure | The word light, which means not heavy
